From fa6b2367e281bc041ce495482dfe11219eab87f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiale Yao <yaojiale02@163.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:15:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: validate RX rate response length

The RX rate query reads a complete PHY information structure without
checking the response length. A truncated firmware response can cause
out-of-bounds reads while decoding the rate.

Require the complete PHY RX information structure before using it.

Fixes: 11553d88d0b9 ("mt76: mt7915: query station rx rate from firmware")
Signed-off-by: Jiale Yao <yaojiale02@163.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261019101506.1926943-9-yaojiale02@163.com
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
index 18acf182..3df809d9 100644
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -4080,6 +4080,10 @@ int mt7915_mcu_get_rx_rate(struct mt7915_phy *phy, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 					&req, sizeof(req), true, &skb);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+	if (skb->len < sizeof(*res)) {
+		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
 
 	res = (struct mt7915_mcu_phy_rx_info *)skb->data;
 
